# Briefcut settings for running from this checkout.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Then put your own key after MODEL_API_KEY= in .env.local.
# .env.local is listed in .gitignore, so it is never committed. This file is
# tracked and must never hold a real key.
#
# Who reads .env.local. Everywhere, a variable already set in your shell wins
# over this file, and an empty value here (like MODEL_API_KEY=) never replaces
# anything, so a key you exported is kept.
#   bash scripts/studio.sh   reads every line below as data. It never runs them.
#   uv run briefcut          (no arguments) reads the first three settings below.
#   uv run vedit doctor      `vedit setup`, `vedit meta status` and `vedit meta check`
#                            read the same three.
#   other uv run vedit ...   commands read nothing from here. Load it first:
#                            set -a; . ./.env.local; set +a
# You can also skip this file and paste the key in Studio under Settings.
#
# A # after a space starts a comment. Keeping comments on their own lines is clearest.

# Your Meta Model API key. Create one at https://dev.meta.ai
# Briefcut sends it only to api.meta.ai.
MODEL_API_KEY=

# 1 allows Meta calls. 0 pauses every Meta call. Footage is sent only when you
# create a story and tick the box that confirms the send.
VEDIT_META_ENABLED=1

# standard or contributor.
#   standard     Muse Spark at the standard price ($1.25 in / $4.25 out per million tokens).
#   contributor  Muse Spark as muse-spark-1.3-contributor, at $0.10 / $0.20 per million
#                tokens. In exchange, Meta may train its future models on what you send
#                to Muse Spark: footage proxies, transcripts, briefs, notes, and caption
#                text. Muse Wonder, SAM 3.1, Muse Image, and Voice Transcribe have no
#                contributor variant and keep their normal prices and terms.
# Leave it on standard for client footage or for people who have not agreed.
VEDIT_META_MODE=standard

# The optional lines below are read only by scripts/studio.sh, or by your shell
# after `set -a; . ./.env.local; set +a`. `uv run briefcut` ignores them.

# Optional. Private mode: glimmer runs director's notes, caption translation and
# script scenes on Muse Glimmer 30B on this computer, through llama.cpp, so
# that text never leaves it. Start the local server first:
#   uv run python -m vedit.open_weights serve
# It fails closed: if the server is not running, those steps stop with an error
# and nothing goes to the Meta API. Everything else still uses the Meta Model API.
# VEDIT_PRIVATE_MODEL=glimmer

# Optional. Who reviews the finished cut: spark (default) or wonder.
# Muse Wonder also listens to the audio. It runs in standard mode only, at $4 in
# and $20 out per million tokens, and needs a project budget of at least $0.33.
# VEDIT_META_DIRECTOR=spark

# Optional. Reasoning effort for Muse Spark: low, medium, or high. Default medium.
# VEDIT_META_REASONING=medium

# Optional. The FFmpeg to use. On a Mac, Homebrew's ffmpeg-full has the filters
# Briefcut needs (drawtext, subtitles). scripts/studio.sh picks it up when it is
# installed, so most people leave this unset.
# VEDIT_FFMPEG=/opt/homebrew/opt/ffmpeg-full/bin/ffmpeg

# Optional. Blender 4.2 or later for 3D motion cards, when it is not on PATH or
# in /Applications. Without Blender the feature is hidden.
# VEDIT_BLENDER=/Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender
